# {{lb|en|transitive|psychology}} To focus one's emotional energies on someone or something.
#* {{quote-book|title=Human Emotions|page=193|author=Carroll E. Izard|year=2013|passage=Apparently it is possible for an individual to '''cathect''' any person, object, idea, or image. Of considerable importance to a possible analogy between cathexis and the emotion of interest, is Freud's notion that an individual can '''cathect''' thought or thinking as well as attention and perception.}}